# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (item 10 of the follow-up): pay, dated in window(03-05, 03-10), is modelled past on its covered
# days and booked on the rest, so whether a binding over transfers holds it is the window's hole: windows each
# splits the count as its pins give it (p3: 0, then 1; p1, p2). 2.1.8's first refcore counted it on every day (1).
# The review's b4_cover_count.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-08
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date

move pay: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03-01..2026-03-07
  known 2026-03-08
  covers konto

ask p1: count(t in transfers over 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31) with wd = 2026-03-05
ask p2: count(t in transfers over 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31) with wd = 2026-03-09
ask p3: count(t in transfers over 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31) windows each
=== expect
p1: 0
  pinned: wd = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-03-08
p2: 1
  pinned: wd = 2026-03-09
  cut 2026-03-08
p3 [wd = 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-07]: 0
  cut 2026-03-08
p3 [wd = 2026-03-08 .. 2026-03-10]: 1
  cut 2026-03-08
